Demo film: 盐城，是从海里长出来的 (Yancheng, grown from the sea). All pictures drawn in code (TypeScript, Remotion 4, SVG).

Data (pre-baked into public/map.json by scripts/prep.py; prep.py's raw inputs are not shipped):
- Coastline, land mask, roads, waterways, county boundaries: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0 (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright).
- Country and province outlines: Natural Earth 1:10m (public domain).
- Historical coastlines (c. 1128 / 1500 / 1600 / 1855), the Yellow River's old course, wind-farm positions: schematic, hand-placed from published maps and papers; marked "示意" on screen.

Font: Noto Serif SC Black (思源宋体 Black), SIL Open Font License 1.1 — not shipped; build.sh copies it from the kit or downloads
  https://github.com/notofonts/noto-cjk/raw/main/Serif/SubsetOTF/SC/NotoSerifSC-Black.otf
Labels: system Noto Sans CJK SC (OFL).
Paper grain: generated by scripts/gen_grain.py.

Music: the user's own track ("老配乐"), not shipped and not licensed for redistribution; build.sh reads it from $MUSIC.
Sound effects: synthesised in scripts/make_audio.py.

Facts on screen (years, 582 km coastline, 2019 World Heritage listing, >10 GW wind) were checked against government and news sources
during production; the scroll quotes 《民国续修盐城县志》 as cited in a paper, not checked against the original book.

Style reference (grammar only, nothing copied): the Douyin account 来龙去脉's dark-brown 2D map explainers.
